DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't chase one day's chip rally.</b> Chips jumped 2.6% and AMD beat, but new lows (128) swamped new highs (38) and Fear & Greed fell to 19.1; one good day doesn't end a correction.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Extreme fear and a narrow market are when regular buying (DCA) in broad funds works best; guessing the bottom rarely does.",
"<b>Don't trade on the election.</b> Results come in today; JPMorgan expects only small moves either way, and post-midterm months have usually been good for patient investors.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> A few giants lifted the S&P while most stocks fell; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on AI.",
"<b>Rates may rise again.</b> Strong job openings pushed December hike odds to about 78% and the 10Y to 4.95%; avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can. Cash and short-term bonds still pay while you wait.",
"<b>Fuel is easing, slowly.</b> Brent is at a four-week low near $104 and US diesel about $6.29, but talks with Iran aren't a deal yet; budget for prices bouncing back.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It slipped to about $3,928, near its low for the year; if you hold some, keep it a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is near $77.7k, ETFs lost about $399M and Binance outflows hit about $4.7B; don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: be patient and selective.</b> The SET (1,491.01) broke 1,500 support even as foreigners bought for a third day; brokers favor defensive names. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 19.1 = Extreme Fear, down from 22.7 on Monday and 32.9 a week ago, even though the S&P rose. Six of the seven signals are in extreme fear; junk-bond demand collapsed to 2."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated, up 2: the US struck an Iranian anti-aircraft site on Qeshm Island and Russia launched one of its largest attacks of the war on Ukraine's grid, though Qatar's US-Iran mediation and the 10-11 Nov Abu Dhabi talks continue."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 14.2 = extreme fear: Tuesday's small gain didn't lift the index far from its lows."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 34.6 = fear (38 NYSE highs vs 128 lows Tuesday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 42.0 = fear, a little better, but most S&P stocks fell Tuesday while chip giants rose."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 18.0 = extreme fear: investors are still buying lots of protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 18.8 = extreme fear: the VIX eased to about 20.8 but stays elevated."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 4.0 = extreme fear: bonds have beaten stocks over recent weeks."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 2.0 = extreme fear, down from 36.4: lenders are demanding more to lend to weaker companies as Big Tech floods the bond market."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 64 (up from 62): the US hit an Iranian anti-aircraft site on Qeshm Island and Iran's negotiator says Iran is 'ready for battle', but Qatar says both sides are reviewing proposals. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 44 (up from 40), the biggest weight: one of the war's largest strikes hit Ukraine's grid and at least 33 died at an aid site, while talks in Abu Dhabi are set for 10-11 Nov."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 70 (unchanged): Hormuz is still effectively shut and the US struck a Hormuz island, but oil kept easing as markets priced less escalation."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 17 (down from 18): Qatar is relaying US-Iran proposals in real time and the Abu Dhabi Ukraine talks are confirmed."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats; Iran's plan would restart talks on its nuclear program."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,569 Tuesday (+0.36%), ending a three-day slide, though most of its stocks fell."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −0.38% Tuesday, weighed down by Apple after its margin forecast."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +0.83% Tuesday as chips rebounded 2.6%; the Nasdaq 100 is still in a correction, about 10% off its high."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.95% Tuesday, its biggest rise since late September, after strong job openings."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$96.1 (−0.4%) Tuesday, its lowest close since 14 Oct, on hopes for a US-Iran deal."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$103.6 (−1.1%) Tuesday, its lowest close since 7 Oct; Hormuz is still effectively shut."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.29/gal (AAA, 3 Nov), edging down and below the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,928 (−0.7%) Tuesday as yields and the dollar rose; it sits near its low for the year and below $4,000."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$77.7k = bearish: it steadied after dipping to about $76.3k, but ETFs lost about $399M and it is on course for a fifth weekly loss."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September. October CPI is due 10 Nov."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 78% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec as of midday 3 Nov, up from about 74%."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. Last noted about 101.8 (2 Nov); the Bloomberg dollar gauge rose 0.3% Tuesday on strong jobs data."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.7 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,491.01 Tue 3 Nov (−1.07%), below 1,500 support; brokers see support at 1,480 and resistance at 1,510 today, with 1,450 next if 1,500 isn't regained."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿633M on 3 Nov, a third straight day of buying; October was about −฿6.6B (our sums of SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
